# Security Standards

Apply these standards when working on security-sensitive code.

- Validate all external input. Never trust user data.
- Use parameterized queries — no string concatenation for SQL/NoSQL.
- Store secrets in environment variables or secret managers, never in code.
- Use standard cryptographic primitives — no custom crypto.
- Error messages must not leak internal details (stack traces, DB schema).
- Always delegate to `/security-reviewer` after completing security-sensitive changes.

